From: Tuth <tuth3378@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 00:02:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 19/24] MS2000: H-bank wild-pc hole-guard - full 30 s run, WAV
 rendered, no crash

MEASURED (bankstorm 30 s, warden 4096 MB):
- The program change at t~6.5 s drives the DSP to the external-P hole
  (two wild pcs seen: 0x800010, 0x900010 - valid 24-bit P addresses, no physical
  backing on the MS2k: internal P ends at 0x18000, boot ROM starts at 0xFF0000).
  Compiling there read unmapped P -> bad_alloc -> std::terminate (the old crash).
- FIX: JitBlockChain::create never compiles in [0x18000, 0xFF0000). A bare
  return froze the machine (measured: 16 billion dispatches, zero cycle
  progress, t= stuck at 6.53 s) - a garbage fetch on silicon still consumes
  cycles and advances the PC, so the guard advances one word + 2 cycles
  (fastForward(1,2) + setPC(_pc+1)). The pending interrupts then come due, the
  ISR runs and its stacked return pulls execution out of the hole - both wild
  pcs were ridden through and the machine recovered, exactly like the real
  synth survives its half-uploaded program changes.

RESULTS:
- Full 30 s emulated run, clean exit, zero terminate, memory flat.
- WAV written: 7.9 MB, 30.0 s, 24-bit stereo. REAL SIGNAL at the first
  program change (t=3-6 s: RMS 0.055/0.057, peak 0.614) - the synth sounds.
  A full-scale transient at the second change, then silence: the hole-walks
  dropped ~116K SHI RX bytes (FIFO overruns while the DSP was in the hole),
  corrupting the second uploaded program. Next: why the SHI IRQ is not
  serviced during the walks (interrupt-func state instrument added).
---
 source/dsp56kEmu/jitblockchain.cpp | 23 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+)

diff --git a/source/dsp56kEmu/jitblockchain.cpp b/source/dsp56kEmu/jitblockchain.cpp
index 09f4319e..c0ed2f54 100644
--- a/source/dsp56kEmu/jitblockchain.cpp
+++ b/source/dsp56kEmu/jitblockchain.cpp
@@ -191,6 +191,29 @@ namespace dsp56k
 	// to the trampoline on a flat stack, and the next execOne picks up the freshly compiled block
 	const bool runFromHere = _execute && !g_inFuncCreate;
 
+	// 2026-10-13 H-bank wild-pc ride-through: the MS2k program change drives the PC into the
+	// external-P hole (measured pc 0x800010 - a valid 24-bit P address with no physical backing on
+	// this machine: internal P is 0x18000 words, the boot ROM starts at 0xFF0000). On real silicon
+	// the half-uploaded program's transient wild jumps ride through: the garbage fetch still
+	// consumes cycles and advances the PC, the pending interrupts come due, and the ISR's stacked
+	// return pulls execution out of the hole. A bare return here froze the machine instead
+	// (measured: 16 billion dispatches, zero cycle progress, t= stuck at 6.53 s), so mirror the
+	// silicon: never compile in the hole, but advance one fetched word and its cycles.
+	if (_pc >= 0x18000 && _pc < 0xFF0000)
+	{
+		static thread_local int s_holeCreate = 0;
+		if ((++s_holeCreate & 1048575) == 1)
+		{
+			const auto& intF = m_jit.dsp().getInterruptFunc();
+			std::fprintf(stderr, "[JIT] create: pc 0x%06X in the external-P hole - advancing; interruptFunc=%p isPeriph=%d\n",
+				_pc, *reinterpret_cast<void* const*>(&intF),
+				intF == m_jit.dsp().getExecPeripheralsFunc() ? 1 : 0);
+		}
+		m_jit.dsp().fastForward(1, 2);
+		m_jit.dsp().setPC(_pc + 1);
+		return;
+	}
+
 //		LOG("Create @ " << HEX(_pc));// << std::endl << cacheEntry.block->getDisasm());
 
 		ensureCacheSize(_pc+1);
